<title>USA: U.S. rev Q1 corporate profits +2.9 pct (+3.5).</title>
<headline>U.S. rev Q1 corporate profits +2.9 pct (+3.5).</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department released on Thursday estimates of profits by U.S. corporations to reflect annual revisions. Profits before tax include inventory valuation and capital consumption adjustments.</p>
<p>Data are chain-weighted and expressed in seasonally adjusted annual rates of billions of dollars, with first quarter percent changes from the fourth quarter. Previously reported estimates follow current data.  </p>
<p> -		   Pct--Q1'97--Prev---Q4'96---Prev---1996---Prev</p>
<p> -  After Tax    2.9  467.2  422.3  454.0   408.2  447.6  406.8</p>
<p> -  Before Tax   4.3  779.6  712.5  747.8   670.1  735.9  670.2</p>
<p> Tax Liability   6.7  241.2  246.2  226.0   228.9  229.0  233.0</p>
</text>
